From 515458596dc4c17d7c3acc0a39e5f7e024272b31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: li-yiyang <yiyang.li.11pro@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 11:20:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] mmc: sdhci-msm: calibrate the BH201 SD retimer for SDR104

The microSD slot on the Lenovo Y700 (TB323FU) has an O2Micro/BayHub BH201
retimer between the SDHCI controller and the card.  The retimer drives its
own TX DLL (sela and selb, 11 phases each, with separate 100m and 200m
configurations).  At 202 MHz the phase that samples this card correctly is
not the same on every power-up, and sdhci-msm's tuning only moves the
controller's RX phase: a wrong 200m phase still passes the host tuning,
but every data read fails with a CRC error.

The vendor kernel calibrates that phase in place: write a phase at 202 MHz,
read the retimer's status registers, score it.  Neither half works on this
unit.  The status read (CMD7(0), CMD17 with argument 0, CMD7(0), CMD7 with
the RCA) returns noise and a CRC error on the reselect, which is why the
Android driver reports "pass windows too small" and falls back to high
speed; and a run of 202 MHz phase writes eventually stops being accepted,
so the recovery needs a card re-init.

Use the vendor's other recovery mechanism instead: write the candidate
configuration at 400 kHz from init_card, let the core re-enumerate the
card, and score the phase by reading LBA0 through the real 202 MHz link.
The host's own execute_tuning() runs before every score, because
sdhci-msm initializes its CM DLL and enables clock-data-recovery only from
there; without it every phase fails.  The sweep covers all 121
(sela, selb) pairs, ranks the widest passing runs, verifies the best four
on fresh enumerations and drops SDR104 (SDR50 still works) if none of
them reads.  The phase map moves with the DLL re-lock, so the sweep runs
at every boot; it costs about 40 s.  A later attach - a system resume
re-initialises the registered card in place - only re-scores the stored
phase, because a sweep there would delete the block device under a
mounted root filesystem.

Signed-off-by: li-yiyang <yiyang.li.11pro@outlook.com>
---
 drivers/mmc/host/Kconfig         |  17 +
 drivers/mmc/host/Makefile        |   1 +
 drivers/mmc/host/sd-retimer-o2.c | 895 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/mmc/host/sd-retimer-o2.h |  15 +
 drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-msm.c     |   3 +
 5 files changed, 931 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/mmc/host/sd-retimer-o2.c
 create mode 100644 drivers/mmc/host/sd-retimer-o2.h

