+	depends on MMC_SDHCI_MSM=y
+	help
+	  Say Y here to calibrate the O2Micro/BayHub BH201 SD retimer
+	  that sits between the SDHCI controller and the card on some
+	  boards (for example the Lenovo Y700 TB323FU, whose table this
+	  driver carries).  The driver writes the board's configuration
+	  at card init time and calibrates the retimer's 200 MHz TX phase
+	  by re-enumerating the card once per candidate phase and reading
+	  a known block over the real 202 MHz link.  The retimer's phase
+	  map moves with every DLL re-lock, so the sweep runs at boot and
